From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anthony Fu <github@antfu.me>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 13:25:26 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] feat(server): accept subdomain wildcards in CORS allowed
 origins

The origin allowlist only took exact origins or `*`. With several web UIs
on one private domain (e.g. a Tailscale tailnet), each has its own origin,
so every daemon had to list each one, and `*` lets any website reach the
daemon from the browser. An entry like `https://*.example.com` now accepts
any subdomain of example.com on that scheme and port, for both the
websocket upgrade and the HTTP CORS headers.

Fork-Change: F-8
